<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>DVD Logo Bounce</title>
    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background-color: #1a1a2e;
            color: white;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        #container {
            width: 80%;
            height: 70%;
            border: 2px solid #4a4e69;
            position: relative;
            background-color: #0f3460;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        .dvd-logo {
            font-family: 'Arial', sans-serif;
            font-size: 24px;
            font-weight: bold;
            color: #e94560;
            position: absolute;
            user-select: none;
            white-space: nowrap;
        }

        .dvd-logo span {
            display: inline-block;
            transform-origin: center;
        }

        .circle {
            border-radius: 50%;
            padding: 2px 8px;
            background-color: #e94560;
            color: white;
            font-size: 16px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div id="container">
    <div class="dvd-logo" id="logo">
        <span class="circle">DVD</span><br>Digital Video Disc
    </div>
</div>

<script>
    const logo = document.getElementById('logo');
    const container = document.getElementById('container');

    let x, y, dx, dy;
    const speed = 3; // pixels per frame

    function init() {
        const rect = container.getBoundingClientRect();
        const width = rect.width - 40;
        const height = rect.height - 20;

        x = width / 2;
        y = height / 2;
        dx = speed * (Math.random() > 0.5 ? 1 : -1);
        dy = speed * (Math.random() > 0.5 ? 1 : -1);
    }

    function update() {
        x += dx;
        y += dy;

        const rect = container.getBoundingClientRect();
        const width = rect.width - 40;
        const height = rect.height - 20;

        // Bounce off walls
        if (x <= 0 || x + logo.offsetWidth >= width) {
            dx *= -1;
            x = Math.max(0, Math.min(x, width - logo.offsetWidth));
        }

        if (y <= 0 || y + logo.offsetHeight >= height) {
            dy *= -1;
            y = Math.max(0, Math.min(y, height - logo.offsetHeight));
        }

        logo.style.left = x + 'px';
        logo.style.top = y + 'px';

        requestAnimationFrame(update);
    }

    window.addEventListener('resize', init);
    init();
    update();
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

**How it works:**

- **HTML/CSS**: Creates a dark-themed container with the DVD logo (text-based: "DVD" in a red circle above "Digital Video Disc").
- **JavaScript**: Uses `requestAnimationFrame` for smooth animation. The logo moves at a constant speed (`dx`, `dy`) and reverses direction when hitting any wall by negating the velocity component. Position clamping prevents it from getting stuck outside the container.

**To use:** Save as an `.html` file and open in any browser. The logo will bounce continuously across the screen without gravity or friction.
